96	// initialStates: additional states seeded into the BFS frontier alongside
97	// init() — the versioning use (docs/VERSIONING.md, polyvers): explore the
98	// machine's rules FROM live fleet snapshots, so "can any currently existing
99	// instance be driven to a violation" becomes the same exhaustive check as
100	// "is the machine correct from init". Seeds dedupe against init and each
101	// other by stable(); counterexample paths record whether they start at init
102	// or at a seed.
103	// steps: an explicit (action, data) domain override — [{action, data}] — used
104	// by callers that must explore two modules over the SAME alphabet (polynv's
105	// mutation grade drives adapter-wrapped mutants with the original module's
106	// manifest domain). When provided it replaces domain building entirely; the
107	// caller owns alphabet correctness.
108	// Live progress/warning writes must never crash the check: a consumer that
109	// closed stderr mid-run (`2>&1 | head`) raises EPIPE on write.
110	const stderrLine = (line) => { try { process.stderr.write(line + '\n'); } catch { /* closed pipe */ } };
