326	    // Drift is about what exploration MINTS, so only init and BFS-discovered
327	    // states feed the detector. Seeded states are excluded on BOTH sides: a
328	    // fleet corpus (polyvers seeds every snapshot) carrying a per-instance
329	    // distinct key — an id, a timestamp — would otherwise inflate the
330	    // numerator past a denominator that already excludes seeds and flag a
331	    // perfectly bounded machine as unbounded.
