433	  // ── Frozen-field scan ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
434	  // A state key whose value is identical across EVERY reachable state (init,
435	  // seeds, and everything BFS discovered) is invisible to this check: any
436	  // behavior gated on a non-default value of that key is structurally
437	  // unreachable from init, and the invariants pass vacuously over it. This is
438	  // not hypothetical — deleting a safety gate guarded by such a key still
439	  // model-checks clean (eval/FINDING-raft-field-study.md, `startIndex`). The
440	  // remedy is --initial-states seeding (or traces) with a non-default value;
441	  // seeded states join `parent`, so an unfreezing seed clears the warning by
442	  // construction. Reported as its own field, NOT in domainNotes: downstream
