477	  // statesExplored counts what exploration DISCOVERED (init + BFS finds);
478	  // seeded roots are reported separately so a seeded run cannot overstate
479	  // its coverage by counting states it was merely handed.
480	  // ── Rejection coverage (the specialRules cross-check) ─────────────────────
481	  // The contract's specialRules are rendered into the generation prompt as
482	  // REQUIRED reject(reason) cases and verified by REPLAY against whatever
483	  // windows the corpus happens to contain. This is the exhaustive-tier half:
484	  // over the whole explored graph, did each declared rejection actually fire
485	  // with its declared reason? A declared rule that never fires is either
486	  // unreachable over the explored domain or mis-reasoned in the code — both
